@startuml requirement-issue-agent-starts
' cumin works - states of a requirement issue: which transitions start an agent,
' which of them read the quota usage first, and what cumin does while it stops after the current runs.
' The states and the transitions are the ones of requirement-issue-states.puml; only the names are shown.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
state "ready" as Ready
state "planning" as Planning
state "awaiting-plan-review" as PlanReview
state "implementing" as Implementing
state "accepting" as Accepting
state "awaiting-acceptance" as Acceptance
state "awaiting-decision" as Decision

[*] --> Draft
Draft -[#888888,dashed]-> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Draft -[#888888]-> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work
Ready -[#D32F2F,bold]-> Planning : <color:#D32F2F>request the split</color>
Planning -[#888888]-> PlanReview : ask the Owner to review the plan
Planning -[#1565C0,bold]-> Accepting : <color:#1565C0>request the acceptance check</color>
Planning -[#D32F2F,bold]-> Planning : <color:#D32F2F>request the split again</color>
Planning -[#888888]-> Decision : stop the split for the Owner
PlanReview -[#888888]-> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work
Implementing -[#1565C0,bold]-> Accepting : <color:#1565C0>request the acceptance check</color>
Implementing -[#888888]-> PlanReview : ask the Owner about the remaining sub-issues
Accepting -[#888888]-> Acceptance : ask the Owner to accept
Accepting -[#D32F2F,bold]-> Accepting : <color:#D32F2F>request the acceptance check again</color>
Accepting -[#888888]-> Decision : stop the acceptance check for the Owner
Acceptance -[#888888]-> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work
Acceptance -[#888888,dashed]-> [*] : the Owner closes the issue
Decision -[#888888,dashed]-> Ready : the Owner adds ready

legend right
  <color:#D32F2F>**Red**</color>: cumin starts an agent, and reads the quota usage first. At a limit, cumin starts nothing
  and counts nothing; the issue keeps its state, and a later poll decides again.
  <color:#1565C0>**Blue**</color>: cumin starts an agent, and reads no usage: an issue in work goes on.
  Gray: cumin starts no agent (a label, a comment, a notification). Dashed: the Owner acts.

  While cumin stops after the current runs (cumin stop --after-current-runs):
  cumin takes no red and no blue transition; the issue keeps its state until the next start.
  cumin still takes the gray transitions.
endlegend

@enduml
